WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.738
Across Wrocław, bronze dwarves share

00:00:02.738 --> 00:00:04.312
poses and props.

00:00:04.312 --> 00:00:06.025
Given a photograph, which individual

00:00:06.025 --> 00:00:07.750
statue are we looking at?

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:11.147
Meet Doppeldwarf-306.

00:00:11.692 --> 00:00:14.079
A frozen vision model turns each image

00:00:14.079 --> 00:00:16.392
into a vector: a numerical visual

00:00:16.392 --> 00:00:17.554
description.

00:00:17.554 --> 00:00:20.517
Cosine similarity compares these vectors.

00:00:20.517 --> 00:00:22.567
Similar directions suggest similar

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:23.417
appearance;

00:00:23.417 --> 00:00:25.242
they do not prove identity.

00:00:25.242 --> 00:00:27.242
We rank each statue by its best

00:00:27.242 --> 00:00:28.929
reference photograph, without

00:00:28.929 --> 00:00:30.647
fine-tuning the model.

00:00:31.242 --> 00:00:33.092
Now add more candidates.

00:00:33.092 --> 00:00:35.304
Do lookalikes overwhelm retrieval?

00:00:35.304 --> 00:00:37.667
Instead of reporting one accuracy number,

00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.792
we repeatedly sample larger candidate

00:00:39.792 --> 00:00:41.742
pools, always keeping the correct

00:00:41.742 --> 00:00:42.992
statue.

00:00:42.992 --> 00:00:45.654
DINOv2's accuracy falls slowly;

00:00:45.654 --> 00:00:47.279
CLIP's falls faster.

00:00:47.279 --> 00:00:49.247
The curve is the result.

00:00:49.817 --> 00:00:51.892
Surely location solves this?

00:00:51.892 --> 00:00:53.829
But nearby lookalikes survive a hard

00:00:53.829 --> 00:00:55.454
geographic filter.

00:00:55.454 --> 00:00:58.092
In simulation, a soft distance bonus

00:00:58.092 --> 00:00:59.329
works better.

00:00:59.329 --> 00:01:02.054
Across 294 placed statues,

00:01:02.054 --> 00:01:03.692
DINOv2 rises from

00:01:03.692 --> 00:01:06.742
93.4 to 98.7

00:01:06.742 --> 00:01:08.892
percent for users twenty-five metres

00:01:08.892 --> 00:01:10.513
away.

00:01:11.058 --> 00:01:12.633
A new photographer brings different

00:01:12.633 --> 00:01:15.196
viewpoints, backgrounds, and lighting.

00:01:15.196 --> 00:01:16.446
Accuracy drops;

00:01:16.446 --> 00:01:18.208
fewer reference photographs also

00:01:18.208 --> 00:01:19.408
contribute.

00:01:19.408 --> 00:01:21.683
LoFTR matches local details across

00:01:21.683 --> 00:01:22.883
photographs.

00:01:22.883 --> 00:01:25.433
Geometric consistency adds evidence to

00:01:25.433 --> 00:01:27.458
visual similarity, moving a better

00:01:27.458 --> 00:01:29.247
match up the shortlist.

00:01:29.792 --> 00:01:32.092
Finally, high similarity need not mean

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:33.554
a known statue.

00:01:33.554 --> 00:01:35.279
Comparing the best two candidates

00:01:35.279 --> 00:01:37.154
exposes ambiguity.

00:01:37.154 --> 00:01:39.479
This margin reduces false acceptance in

00:01:39.479 --> 00:01:40.517
the research;

00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:42.679
the browser demo uses a separately

00:01:42.679 --> 00:01:44.647
measured close-call hint.

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:47.254
The lesson: test the pool, the place,

00:01:47.254 --> 00:01:48.654
and the photographer.

00:01:48.654 --> 00:01:50.404
Explore the dataset, and try the

00:01:50.404 --> 00:01:51.880
identifier.
